Subject: [PATCH] NetworkPkg/TcpDxe: open the IP child BY_CHILD for an accepted socket

TcpAttachPcb() opens each socket's own IP instance BY_CHILD_CONTROLLER
for the socket's handle. A connection a listener accepts gets its TCB
from TcpCloneTcb(), which shares the listener's IpInfo (a reference,
NET_GET_REF) but never opens that IP instance for the new socket's
handle. When the IP instance is stopped (a Shell `reconnect -r`, or a
disconnect of the NIC, with an accepted connection alive), the DXE
core hands TcpDxe's Stop() only the children that opened it: the
listener. Stop() destroys the listener and returns success; the
accepted socket's reference keeps the IpInfo, so the IP instance stays
open BY_DRIVER, and CoreDisconnectControllersUsingProtocolInterface()
calls Stop() again, forever, at TPL_CALLBACK.

TcpCloneTcb() now opens the shared IP instance BY_CHILD_CONTROLLER for
the clone's socket, as TcpAttachPcb() does. Stop() is then handed the
accepted socket too and destroys it; SockDestroyChild() already closes
Tcb->IpInfo->ChildHandle for the socket's handle (a close that, for an
accepted socket, failed until now). If the open fails, the clone is
destroyed and TcpCloneTcb() fails, as it does when SockClone() fails.

When SockClone() fails (a listener at its backlog), TcpCloneTcb() now
returns the IpInfo reference it took. The reference was leaked, and one
left behind keeps the IP instance open after its listener is gone, so
that its disconnect calls Stop() forever in the same way.

axl-firmware's patch against edk2-stable202611, applied after
0012-localapic-eoi.patch to a copy of the packages it touches.

---
diff --git a/NetworkPkg/TcpDxe/TcpMisc.c b/NetworkPkg/TcpDxe/TcpMisc.c
index 3310306..4e8d04f 100644
--- a/NetworkPkg/TcpDxe/TcpMisc.c
+++ b/NetworkPkg/TcpDxe/TcpMisc.c
@@ -535,7 +535,11 @@ TcpCloneTcb (
   IN TCP_CB  *Tcb
   )
 {
-  TCP_CB  *Clone;
+  TCP_CB      *Clone;
+  IP_IO       *IpIo;
+  EFI_GUID    *IpProtocolGuid;
+  VOID        *Ip;
+  EFI_STATUS  Status;
 
   Clone = AllocateZeroPool (sizeof (TCP_CB));
 
@@ -557,12 +561,55 @@ TcpCloneTcb (
   Clone->Sk = SockClone (Tcb->Sk);
   if (Clone->Sk == NULL) {
     DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "TcpCloneTcb: failed to clone a sock\n"));
+    //
+    // Return the reference taken above: a reference left behind keeps the
+    // IP instance open after its listener is gone, and its disconnect then
+    // calls Stop() forever.
+    //
+    NET_PUT_REF (Tcb->IpInfo);
     FreePool (Clone);
     return NULL;
   }
 
   ((TCP_PROTO_DATA *)(Clone->Sk->ProtoReserved))->TcpPcb = Clone;
 
+  //
+  // Open the shared IP instance BY_CHILD for the clone's socket, as
+  // TcpAttachPcb() does for a socket of its own, so that when the IP
+  // instance is stopped (a NIC disconnect or reconnect), the driver's Stop()
+  // is handed this socket among the children and destroys it.
+  // SockDestroyChild() closes it. Without it, Stop() never sees the socket,
+  // its reference keeps the IP instance open BY_DRIVER, and the
+  // disconnect of that instance calls Stop() forever.
+  //
+  if (Clone->Sk->IpVersion == IP_VERSION_4) {
+    IpProtocolGuid = &gEfiIp4ProtocolGuid;
+  } else {
+    IpProtocolGuid = &gEfiIp6ProtocolGuid;
+  }
+
+  IpIo   = ((TCP_PROTO_DATA *)(Clone->Sk->ProtoReserved))->TcpService->IpIo;
+  Status = gBS->OpenProtocol (
+                  Clone->IpInfo->ChildHandle,
+                  IpProtocolGuid,
+                  &Ip,
+                  IpIo->Image,
+                  Clone->Sk->SockHandle,
+                  EFI_OPEN_PROTOCOL_BY_CHILD_CONTROLLER
+                  );
+  if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
+    DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "TcpCloneTcb: failed to open the IP instance for a sock: %r\n", Status));
+    //
+    // Destroying the sock detaches the clone, which drops its reference on
+    // the IpInfo and frees it. The clone is on no TCB list yet, and has no
+    // token: destroy it as unconfigured, so that nothing removes it from a
+    // list it is not on.
+    //
+    Clone->Sk->ConfigureState = SO_UNCONFIGURED;
+    SockDestroyChild (Clone->Sk);
+    return NULL;
+  }
+
   return Clone;
 }
 
